  "evidence": [
    "Bounded detached Matrix upload input survives caller collection mutation during provider I/O. Counts-only requests neither reserve nor acknowledge any identity.",
    "Signed own-device identity is reserved and journaled before upload; retained LEGACY fingerprint replacement is rejected. Signed ephemeral keys without supplied identity require a published identity.",
    "Each outside-SQL provider read/upload/readback has current account/native/group/client/MFA/canonical device/provider generation/exact request checks before and after either provider outcome, under the original clipped30-second budget.",
    "Matching signed readback can atomically acknowledge only the exact reservation and journal, with readback/final admission. Competing same-identity uploads acknowledge once; version1 metadata cannot change during replay.",
    "Lost upload response, cancellation, journal/post-write failure, native purge or changed native/provider generation preserve the owned uncertain reservation. Exact final release cannot erase a replacement request.",
